            <ArticleTitle>Referred pain of muscular origin resembling endodontic involvement. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>223-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Referred pain is common in the orofacial region and can cause considerable difficulties in diagnosis. Referred pain is defined as pain that is referred to a part of the body other than the site of origin, and as a result, severe pain may arise without an associated causative lesion. A muscular trigger point that resembled a tooth with endodontic involvement is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
